{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Thus.</b> I am He who formed Israel:" "<b>Ask Me.</b> Imperative mood, like <i>hear me</i> and <i>plead for me</i> (Genesis 23:8), on account of the gutteral sign." "<b>Will you command Me?</b> In astonishment: does not the Maker know what He makes? Are not Israel My children, and behold you command Me to speak with the nations of the world?"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:09.666059876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}